\title{edgeicg: Spillover-Aware Interaction-Changed Genes at Contact, Paracrine and Niche Scale}
\description{
Tests whether a receiver cell type changes a gene's expression with its exposure to a sender cell type, at three spatial scales: touching cells (contact), short-range neighbours (paracrine) and the regional neighbourhood (niche). Transcripts leaked from touching neighbours are modelled from the data and removed per cell before testing. Niche effects are screened with a calibrated marginal test (toroidal-shift null) and attributed to senders by exact fine-mapping. Counts are read in gene blocks through a provider, so whole sections run in bounded memory, in memory or from a disk-backed store, sequentially or on 'mirai' daemons.
